lt true.\n\nFor reactions via Plugin API: node.reactions = [{ action: { type: 'NODE', destinationId: 'xx', navigation: 'NAVIGATE', transition: {type:'SMART_ANIMATE'...} or null, ... }, trigger: { type: 'ON_CLICK' } }]. For after-delay: trigger {type:'AFTER_TIMEOUT', timeout: 0.8}. Transition null → instant? Provide transition: { type: 'DISSOLVE', duration: 0.3, easing: {type:'EASE_OUT'} } etc. For simple: transition: null means instant. PUSH transition for go-to product could be nice but keep simple: dissolve/push. I'll use SMART_ANIMATE where reasonable; note: SMART_ANIMATE requires matching layer names ideally but works regardless.\n\nReaction action structure: { type: \"NODE\", destinationId, navigation: \"NAVIGATE\", transition, preserveScrollPosition: false, overlayRelativePosition: null, resetVideoPosition: false, resetScrollPosition: false, resetInteractiveComponents: false } — only some required. Minimal: { type: 'NODE', destinationId, navigation: 'NAVIGATE', transition: null }. I think transition: null is valid (instant).\n\nFor setting reactions, destination must be a top-level frame? destinationId can be any frame.\n\nLet me also handle 'SWAP' navigation for overlays — not needed.\n\nOK let me also double check the `symbol` type in metadata = COMPONENT. Yes.\n\nOne more inspection: I should look at the components page screenshot to match default button style (I have exact specs from dump — orange #FFA451 r=1,g=0.643,b=0.3176 = FFA451, radius 10, Nunito SemiBold 16 white). Text Field: #F3F1F1-ish (0.953,0.945,0.945 ≈ #F3F1F1), radius 10, placeholder 16 Regular #C1BDBD. Good.\n\nNow write Script A. Positions on workspace page: I'll place components section at x=0, y=3000 area; screens at:\nRow1 y=0: 01 x=0, 02 x=455, 03 x=910, 04 x=1365\nRow2 y=892: 05 x=0, 06 x=455, 07 x=910, 08 x=1365\nRow3 y=1784: 09 x=0, 10 x=455\nComponents at y=2676, x=0.. \n\nSpacing 80 between frames.\n\nActually wait — workspace page currently empty (no children). Good.\n\nLet me write Script A now:\n\n```js\nvar page = figma.getNodeById('9:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\n// fonts\nvar fonts = [\n  {family:'Nunito', style:'Regular'},\n  {family:'Nunito', style:'SemiBold'},\n  {family:'Nunito', style:'Bold'},\n  {family:'Nunito', style:'ExtraBold'}\n];\nfor (var f of fonts) { try { await figma.loadFontAsync(f); } catch(e){ return 'FONT FAIL '+f.style+' '+e.message; } }\n// clone given components\nvar ids = {button:'3:25', field:'3:28', status:'3:32', home:'3:42'};\nvar out = {};\nvar x = 0;\nfor (var k in ids) {\n  var c = figma.getNodeById(ids[k]);\n  var cl = c.clone();\n  page.appendChild(cl);\n  cl.x = x; cl.y = 2600;\n  out[k] = cl.id;\n  x += cl.width + 60;\n}\nreturn JSON.stringify(out);\n```\n\nThen Script B builds components using helpers. Components created via figma.createComponent(). I'll define helper functions in each script (they don't persist across calls).\n\nLet me think about text creation helper:\n\n```js\nfunction txt(chars, size, style, color, parent, x, y, w) {\n  var t = figma.createText();\n  t.fontName = {family:'Nunito', style: style};\n  t.characters = chars;\n  t.fontSize = size;\n  t.fills = [{type:'SOLID', color: color}];\n  if (w) { t.textAutoResize = 'HEIGHT'; t.resize(w, t.height); }\n  t.x = x; t.y = y;\n  parent.appendChild(t);\n  return t;\n}\n```\nNote: must set fontName before characters. Order: createText (default font Inter Regular loaded? createText requires font loaded for default Inter — if not loaded, error. To be safe load Inter Regular too... createText starts with \"a\"? Actually createText creates empty text with default font; setting fontName after. Common pattern: t.fontName = ... then t.characters. If createText itself fails due to Inter not loaded... In practice createText works without loading Inter? The initial text has no characters so no font load needed. Setting fontName requires that font loaded. OK load only Nunito styles. I'll preload in every script that touches text (