ecolor? Icon_Step_Done is likely green check circle; keep original colors.\n11. Step Row / Current (327×84): bg TINT radius 16; icon tile 44 white radius12 at (12,12) with Step_Order_Delivering 36; title 16 Bold INK (68, 16); subtitle \"Your delivery agent is coming\" 12 Regular GRAY (68, 40); right: \"now\" badge? Add small orange dot or \"Current\" label. I'll add pill \"Now\" orange white text at right.\n12. Step Row / Pending (327×56): icon tile LIGHT gray with Icon_Step_Done recolored #C7C7C7; title \"Order Received\" 16 SemiBold #B0B0B0; right: nothing or gray clock. Keep clean.\n\n13. Quantity Stepper (~140×40): Icon_Minus 32 at left, \"1\" 16 Bold centered, Icon_Plus 32 right, then \"pack\" text? Brief: \"1 pack\". I'll do: minus btn, text \"1\" w=24 centered, plus btn, and \"pack\" label after? Cleaner: [−] 1 [+] with \"pack\" as part of qty text: \"1 pack\" 16 SemiBold width ~52 centered. Width: 32+8+56+8+32=136.\n\n14. Sheet / Delivery (375×470): build with fields and buttons. Fields: use Text Field component clones? The Text Field component (cloned) — I'll instantiate `Text Field` component and override text + color for filled state. Filled state: text INK 16 Regular. Label above each: 16 SemiBold INK.\n\n15. Sheet / Card (375×520).\n\nSheets contain instances of Button and Text Field components → nested instances fine.\n\nAlso `Header / Title`? For basket/track headers I have orange band with back pill + title — build inline per screen (it's just back pill component + text).\n\nAlso Status Bar/Home Indicator clones are components already (cloned). I'll instantiate per screen. On dark/orange screens override: status bar instance fills transparent; but children (9:41 text etc.) black — on orange, black text OK-ish. Keep white fill? On 01_Splash full orange, a white status bar strip looks like part of design... The original kit's splash is full orange without visible status bar. I'll include status bar instance but set its fill to orange/transparent so it blends: override fills = []. Transparent fill on instance: fills = [] allowed? For instances you can set fills override yes. Then black 9:41 on orange — readable enough, and \"not part of your design\".\n\nOK. Script A first. Also I realize creating components on the workspace page directly is fine.\n\nOne concern: `figma.getNodeById('9:2')` returns PageNode; setCurrentPageAsync required for createInstance to place on that page? createInstance() adds to currentPage. I'll set current page to workspace in every script that creates instances.\n\nAlso: when cloning components from other pages, clone() keeps parent (original page), then appendChild to workspace page moves it. Good.\n\nLet me write Script A now. Also create paint styles (design tokens) — quick:\n- Brand / Primary FFA451\n- Brand / Tint FFF2E5\n- Text / Primary 262626\n- Text / Secondary 8B8888\n- Surface / Field F3F1F1\n- Semantic / Success 4BB462\n\nI'll add them in Script A.\n\nAfter building, screenshots for verification.\n\nLet me get going. Script A:\n\nAlso note — whoami confirmed zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai. \n\nScript A code:\n\n```js\nvar page = figma.getNodeById('9:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nvar styles = ['Regular','SemiBold','Bold','ExtraBold'];\nfor (var i=0;i<styles.length;i++){ await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Nunito', style:styles[i]}); }\n// color styles\nfunction paint(name, r,g,b){ var s = figma.createPaintStyle(); s.name = name; s.paints = [{type:'SOLID', color:{r:r,g:g,b:b}}]; return s.id; }\nvar ids = {};\nids.primary = paint('Brand/Primary', 1, 0.6431, 0.3176);\nids.tint = paint('Brand/Tint', 1, 0.949, 0.898);\nids.ink = paint('Text/Primary', 0.149, 0.149, 0.149);\nids.gray = paint('Text/Secondary', 0.545, 0.533, 0.533);\nids.field = paint('Surface/Field', 0.953, 0.945, 0.945);\nids.success = paint('Semantic/Success', 0.294, 0.706, 0.384);\n// clone given components\nfunction cloneTo(id, name, x, y){\n  var c = figma.getNodeById(id).clone();\n  page.appendChild(c); c.x = x; c.y = y; c.name = name;\n  return c.id;\n}\nvar out = {};\nout.button = cloneTo('3:25', 'Button / Primary', 0, 2600);\nout.field = cloneTo('3:28', 'Text Field', 387, 2600);\nout.status = cloneTo('3:32', 'Shell / Status Bar', 774, 2600);\nout.home = cloneTo('3:42', 'Shell / Home Indicator', 774, 2660);\nreturn JSON.stringify(out);\n```\n\nThen Script B: components. This will be a long script; maybe split into B1 (buttons/tabs/search/filter/basket-entry/back pill/stepper) and B2 (cards/rows/sheets). Let me write efficiently.\n\nHelper lib (repeat in each script):\n\n```js\nvar N = function(style){ return {family:'Nunito', style:style}; };\nfunction solid(r,g,b){ return [{type:'SOLID', color:{r,g,b}}]; }\nfunction txt(parent, chars, x, y, size, style, color, w, align){\n  var t = figma.createText();\n  parent.appendChild(t);\n  t.fontName = N(style);\n  t.characters = chars;\n  t.fontSize = size;\n  t.fills = solid(color.r,color.g,color.b);\n  if (w){ t.textAutoResize='HEIGHT'; t.resize(w, t.height); }\n  if (align) t.textAlignHorizontal = align;\n  t.x = x; t.y = y;\n  return t;\n}\nfunction rect(parent, w,h,x,y, color, radius){\n  var r = figma.createRectangle();\n  parent.appendChild(r);\n  r.resize(w,h); r.x=x; r.y=y;\n  if (color) r.fills = solid(color.r,color.g,color.b); else r.fills = [];\n  if (radius!==undefined) r.cornerRadius = radius;\n  return r;\n}\nfunction inst(id, parent, x,y, w,h){\n  var c = figma.getNodeById(id);\n  var i = c.createInstance();\n  parent.appendChild(i); i.x=x; i.y=y;\n  if (w && h) i.resize(w,h);\n  return i;\n}\n```\n\nCareful: createInstance places on current page — then appendChild moves into parent. Good.\n\nShadow effect helper:\n```js\nfunction shadow(node, y, blur, opacity){\n  node.effects = [{type:'DROP_SHADOW', color:{r:0,g:0,b:0,a:opacity||0.06}, offset:{x:0,y:y||4}, radius:blur||16, spread:0, visible:true, blendMode:'NORMAL'}];\n}\n```\n\nNow the components (Script B1):\n\nButton / Outline: comp 327×56 white, stroke