{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":37831,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"04036ae581800a7a88bbef91692bc029","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now build the business components. One call per component, each with its own loadFontAsync (call-local):\n\n1. IconButton/Back (y=120)\n2. CategoryChip (y=190)\n3. ProductCard (y=270) — uses Salad_Quinoa master 12:61\n4. HottestRow (y=460) — uses Salad_Honey_Lime 12:59\n5. BasketRow (y=530) — uses Salad_Quinoa 12:61\n6. StepRow (y=610)\n7. Button/Small (y=690)\n8. Button/Secondary (y=700) reuse\n\nThen screens.\n\nLet me write component 1+2 in one call? They said \"build in manageable sections\". I'll do 2-3 calls: Call A: IconButton/Back + CategoryChip + Button/Small + Button/Secondary. Call B: ProductCard. Call C: HottestRow + BasketRow + StepRow.\n\nColor constants (0-1):\nPRIMARY = {r:1,g:0.6431,b:0.3176}\nTINT = {r:1,g:0.949,b:0.898}\nINK = {r:0.149,g:0.149,b:0.149} (#262626)\nMUTED = {r:0.545,g:0.533,b:0.533}\nFIELD = {r:0.953,g:0.945,b:0.945}\nWHITE = {r:1,g:1,b:1}\nPENDING = {r:0.83,g:0.82,b:0.82}\nSUCCESS = {r:0.294,g:0.706,b:0.384}\n\nText helper inside each call:\n```js\nasync function load(){ var fs=['Regular','SemiBold','Bold','ExtraBold']; for(var i=0;i<fs.length;i++) await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Nunito',style:fs[i]}); }\nfunction T(chars, size, style, color, w){ var t=figma.createText(); t.fontName={family:'Nunito',style:style}; t.fontSize=size; t.characters=chars; t.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:color}]; if(w){t.textAutoResize='HEIGHT'; t.resize(w,t.height);} return t; }\n```\n\nCall A code:\n\nIconButton/Back: frame 40x40, fill white, stroke {0.94,0.94,0.94} 1, radius 12, shadow? subtle. Center Icon_Back instance (12:100). Center: inst.x=(40-10)/2=15, y=(40-20)/2=10.\n\nCategoryChip:\n- Default: w auto → fixed 80 h34, fill white, stroke #EBEBEB, radius 17, text \"Popular\" 14 Regular MUTED centered.\n- Selected: 88x34, fill PRIMARY, text \"Hottest\" 14 SemiBold white, radius 17.\nMake both components; put them side by side. Names: \"Category Chip / Default\", \"Category Chip / Selected\".\n\nButton/Small: 108x44, fill PRIMARY, radius 10, text \"Add to basket\" 12 SemiBold white centered.\n\nButton/Secondary: 327x56, fill white, stroke PRIMARY 1.5, radius 10, text \"Continue shopping\" 16 SemiBold PRIMARY centered.\n\nUse absolute positioning inside frames (no autolayout) to keep it simple: parent frame with fills, child text centered via computed positions (need text width after creation: create text, then set x=(parent.w - t.width)/2). Good.\n\nCall A code below. y positions: base 120. Row: IconButton at x0, Chips at x60, x160, Button/Small x280, Secondary x440. All at y=120 (they're different heights; fine, separate columns).","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"32e1e789-097d-46fb-a2c9-6411f0d5873d","uuid":"5c8ec999-ba79-4f2d-88f5-2030617f7b4c","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:50:17.137Z","thinking_duration_ms":21226}
