{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":47852,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02106ae582d10a7a5b659698ab0d111f","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Can't append to an instance! Right — instances are sealed; you can only override properties of children, not add/remove children. So swapPhoto must not append. Options: hide the old photo (visible=false override) and place a new instance as sibling in the frame (parent s4, at card position + offsets), or override the old photo's size only if same asset — but photo content differs.\n\nAlternative: make photos swappable by using nested components — the correct Figma way: make Salad photos variants? They're separate components. I could create variants in a component set... complex.\n\nSimpler: place the new photo instance directly in s4 positioned over the card photo area, and set old photo's opacity 0 / visible false. visible=false on a nested instance is allowed.\n\nswapPhoto(card, saladId, w, h, parentFrame): \nvar old = card.findOne(...Salad_); old.visible=false;\nvar ni = figma.getNodeById(saladId).createInstance();\ncard.parent.appendChild(ni); ni.x = card.x + old.x; ni.y = card.y + old.y; ni.resize(w,h);\n\nCard parent is s4 (frame). Works. But the photo instance will be appended at top of s4's stack → above card ✓ good (cards above, but photo above fav button too — fav button is at top-right, might overlap photo top area? Photo at x=17..137, fav at 120..146, y 8..34. Berry mango photo y=10..120, x=25..135; fav at x=126..152 y=8..34 → photo overlaps fav region! Photo above would cover the fav button. Need ordering: append photo, then... instances order within s4: card appended first, photo later → photo above card → covers card's fav and add? Add button at x=116..144, y=160..188 vs photo y up to 120 → no. Fav y 8..34 vs photo y 10..120 x 25..135 vs fav x 126..152 → overlap region x 126..135, y 10..34. The Salad images likely have transparent padding, mostly OK, but be safe: re-append the card above photo? No—then card covers photo.\n\nBetter: append photo to s4 first (before cards) — but cards already exist at call time. Alternative: insert photo then move it below the card? There's no z-order move API except appendChild which moves to top. So: append photo, then re-append card (card above), then the fav/add come with card ✓, but then card's white bg covers photo? No—photo is at card's photo area; card above would hide photo behind white bg.\n\nHmm. Simplest: leave old photo visible but swap its image via `scaleFactor`? No.\n\nCleanest correct approach: recreate the card composition manually for the variant — i.e., instead of using the component instance for Tropical/Melon/BerryMango, keep instance and just hide old photo + add new photo positioned exactly, accepting tiny overlap risk with fav. Actually check overlap for Hottest card: photo x=17 y=14 size 120x80 → x 17..137, y 14..94; fav x=120..146, y=8..34. Overlap x 120..137, y 14..34. Salad PNGs have transparent backgrounds typically, so visually fine.\n\nAlternative robust: wrap photo area as its own component \"PhotoSlot\" used inside cards, then variant-swap... no variants.\n\nPragmatic: hide old, add new as sibling, then bring fav above: re-append the fav? Fav is inside the card instance — can't reorder relative to s4 children.\n\nOK do: photo sibling + ensure new photo's frame has clipsContent (instances clip). The Salad photos include their own white/transparent bg? They're photos with circular plate on transparent bg presumably. Overlap area is tiny (17px corner). Fine.\n\nAlso BerryMango photo (12:60) 110x110 at (25,10): overlap with fav (126..152 × 8..34): photo x 25..135 → overlap 126..135 — small corner. Acceptable.\n\nNow, current partial state: the failed call created s4 with content up to t1 creation (t1 texts set, swapPhoto failed). So s4 exists with: shell, menu, basket, labels, greeting, search, filter, chips, q card, t1 card (texts set, photo hidden? no—old photo still there, texts changed). m1 not created, recommended not created.\n\nRather than patch, simplest: remove s4 and rebuild with corrected swapPhoto. s4 id? Created fresh in that call; find by name '04_Home' (previous partial was removed in prior call). Delete and rebuild fully.\n\nCorrection to swapPhoto:\nfunction swapPhoto(card, saladId, w, h){\n  var old=card.findOne(function(n){return n.type==='INSTANCE' && n.name.indexOf('Salad_')===0;});\n  old.visible=false;\n  var ni=figma.getNodeById(saladId).createInstance();\n  card.parent.appendChild(ni);\n  ni.x=card.x+old.x; ni.y=card.y+old.y; ni.resize(w,h);\n}\n\nNote old.x is relative to card — when hidden, x/y still readable ✓.\n\nAlso: hidden old photo — visible=false override allowed ✓.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"32e1e789-097d-46fb-a2c9-6411f0d5873d","uuid":"295c73ea-41e3-4e62-8da6-0023fe8a8fad","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:56:05.465Z","thinking_duration_ms":34015}
